ss.leads to this actor; the factory has a cedar slat: was 0, needed 1; business.cedar_slats is raised only by saw-slats (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.cedar_slats to this actor); mix-leads (the lead works has graphite: was 0, needed 1; business.graphite is raised only by mine-graphite (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.graphite to this actor; the lead works has clay: was 0, needed 1; business.clay is raised only by supply-clay (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.clay to this actor); pack-pencils (the factory has a pencil: was 0, needed 1; business.pencils is raised only by make-pencils (on its actor), buy-pencils (on its actor), restock-shop (on its shop); the factory has a box: was 0, needed 1; nothing ever raises business.boxes); receive-boxes (the shipment contains packed pencils: was 0, needed 0; nothing ever raises shipment.packed_pencils); restock-shop (the carrier has enough packed pencils: was 0, needed 1; business.packed_pencils is raised only by pack-pencils (on its actor), dispatch-boxes (on its to), receive-boxes (on its actor)); saw-slats (the sawmill has a cedar log: was 0, needed 1; business.cedar_logs is raised only by cut-cedar (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.cedar_logs to this actor). For each, make sure some other action produces what its checks need (for example, if goods must be at the next stop before they can move on, give someone an action that brings them there). Nothing in the world ever makes or brings in these, and everyone starts with none, so every step that uses them is impossible: boxes, brass_ferrules, erasers, paint. Give each one a source: an actor whose action makes or supplies it, or a process that renews it at the place it comes from. These goods are made or supplied but no move ever takes them from where they pile up, so the step that needs them nev